<article class="env-lemma" id="0DVW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DVW">Lemma <span data-tag="0DVW">93.6.3</span>.</a> In Example <a href="/tag/0D3K" data-tag="0D3K">93.6.1</a> let $\rho _0 : \Gamma \to \text{GL}_ k(V)$ be a finite dimensional continuous representation. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  T\mathcal{D}\! \mathit{ef}_{V, \rho _0} = H^1(\Gamma , \text{End}_ k(V)) \quad \text{and}\quad \text{Inf}(\mathcal{D}\! \mathit{ef}_{V, \rho _0}) = H^0(\Gamma , \text{End}_ k(V))  \]
</div>
  <p> Thus $\text{Inf}(\mathcal{D}\! \mathit{ef}_{V, \rho _0})$ is always finite dimensional and $T\mathcal{D}\! \mathit{ef}_{V, \rho _0}$ is finite dimensional if $\Gamma $ is topologically finitely generated. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The proof is exactly the same as the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/0DVT" data-tag="0DVT">93.5.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>